WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.267
Everything on Estimates.

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:12.033
Estimates. Every estimate in one list, from the first visit to the won job: drafts, ones out with customers, follow-ups, won and lost.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.967
Start a new estimate. New estimate first asks who it is for. The tour opens it to show you.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:27.933
Find the customer. Type a name, phone or street and click the customer: a new draft estimate opens for them straight away.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:37.867
Not a customer yet?. Add a new customer opens the customer form right here. Saving it adds the customer and opens their new estimate.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:45.133
Name. First and last name, or a company name for commercial work. Only a name is required.

00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:53.200
Phones and email. Cell phone, other phone and email. The email is where the estimate and its follow-ups go.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:02.867
Property address. Where the work is. Type the zip and the town fills itself in. Untick "Bill to the property address" if the bill goes somewhere else.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:15.233
Source, salesperson and CSR. How they found you, who referred them, their salesperson and the office CSR. Stage, type, invoicing and payment terms sit just below.

00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:25.400
Book the visit in the same go. Tick it to put the estimate visit on the salesperson's day with the same save: date, time, who goes and what for.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:32.600
Save customer. Saves the customer and opens their new estimate. The tour doesn't save anything.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.100
Close the form. The x closes the form without saving.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:44.667
Drafts. Estimates written but not sent yet, and what they are worth. Click it to see them on the Open tab.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:50.833
Out with customers. Sent and waiting on a yes or no, with their total value.

00:01:51.333 --> 00:02:00.567
In follow-up. Sent estimates with a follow-up due or planned. With automatic follow-ups on, the reminder emails go by themselves.

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:08.167
Won this year. What you won this year, how many jobs that is, and your close rate (won out of won plus lost).

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:16.233
Open. The list starts on Open: drafts, and sent estimates still waiting on an answer. The number is how many.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:22.767
Follow-ups. Sent estimates with a follow-up due, or the next automatic email planned.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:31.733
Who to chase. The Status column says Follow up, 2nd follow-up or Call them, and shows the next automatic step with its date.

00:02:32.233 --> 00:02:35.800
Won. Every estimate the customer said yes to.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.533
Straight to the job. Job opens the job that was made from that estimate.

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:47.833
Lost. Lost and expired estimates, with the reason given when they were marked lost.

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:51.533
All. Every estimate, whatever its status.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:58.900
Search. Type an estimate number, a title, the customer or the town: the list narrows as you type.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:05.467
Filter by rep. Show one salesperson's estimates only. Any rep shows everyone's.

00:03:05.967 --> 00:03:16.833
The columns. Estimate number, title and customer; status; rep; total; and when it was sent. A long list shows 50 at a time with Previous and Next.

00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:23.833
Open one. Click any row to open the estimate. The tour "Everything on an estimate" walks through it.

00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:29.933
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
